title: >-
  Code and data for: Matched runs, unpaired test: recovering a discarded pairing in a small personalisation comparison, and the registered protocol that found no identity separation
message: If you use this code or data, please cite this archive and the manuscript.
type: dataset
authors:
  - given-names: Zeyu
    family-names: Fu
    email: fuzeyu99@126.com
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0009-0001-8329-0108'
    affiliation: 'Army Medical University, Chongqing, China'
abstract: >-
  Identity and caption-fidelity records, adapter manifests, paired concept-by-seed figures and manuscript source for a re-analysis that recovers the pairing a small diffusion-personalisation comparison discarded, reports what the registered identity endpoint can support, and separates its prompt-fidelity secondary endpoint from the protocol design. The official 1000-step B-LoRA result is absent.
keywords:
  - negative result
  - paired comparison
  - registered protocol
  - statistical power
  - diffusion personalisation
  - low-rank adaptation
  - re-analysis
